// Binary64 libm for woof's facade backends (Metal; the CPU tier links the
// same text), under CUDA's own names.  Never compiled for CUDA: the
// translator (woof/backend/translate) prepends it to a unit that calls one
// of these names with a double, and f64cr.cuh rides along.
//
// exp, log, log10, sin, atan, pow: f64cr.cuh's correctly rounded functions,
// the one answer every conforming platform owes (graded against 240-bit
// mpmath by tests/test_lake_f64cr.py).  CUDA's libdevice is 1-2 ULP and not
// correctly rounded, so these are a known delta against the CUDA build and
// the closest available match to WRF's glibc.
// atan2, hypot, log2, expm1, tanh, tgamma(f), lgamma: Rust libm 0.2.16 transcriptions (MIT; FDLIBM notices
// in licenses/LICENSE-FDLIBM-SunPro.txt), one RN operation per AST node.
